    "body": "files list\r\n\r\n- src/nvim/highlight_group.c\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nThe default color theme readability for some cases due to `NonText` foreground color exactly matching the background color of other elements (`ColorColumn`, `FloatShadow`, `FloatShadowThrough`), which makes text invisible. e.g. selected file in snacks_picker(?)\r\n\r\nBoth light and dark theme is affected:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"774\" height=\"312\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 at 7 34 04 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b7140545-8f6c-40f1-9672-4a0151914130\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"768\" height=\"297\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 at 7 34 30 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1b4cfc5-a2f5-40b8-8549-33bc7ee40209\" />\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nChange foreground color to the one from the main text colors of the color scheme, so they make clearly visible pair:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"772\" height=\"309\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 at 7 35 21 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1abd24de-27b5-4c4d-a774-0417fbc9a15a\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"767\" height=\"300\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-30 at 7 35 39 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6861937d-7972-464f-a9bd-2cc87774af83\" />\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-30T18:22:37Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\n> The default color theme readability for some cases due to `NonText` foreground color exactly matching the background color of other elements (`ColorColumn`, `FloatShadow`, `FloatShadowThrough`), which makes text invisible. e.g. selected file in snacks_picker(?)\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a reasonable change for at least the following reasons:\r\n\r\n- Changing foreground from `Nvim{Dark,Light}Grey4` to `Nvim{Light,Dark}Grey4` will make the highlight group be the same as `Comment`, which is a very bad effect to have. The `NonText` is closer to the UI element than text, so it is better to use the grey shade that is closer to the background.\r\n- The three listed groups look like the only ones that can cause trouble here. The both shadow are rather rare to cause the trouble (relatively unpopular and floating window should end just beside the `NonText` group). Although the `ColorColumn` is not great, it is also not very frequent for the same reasons.\r\n- The conflict in 'snacks.nvim' seems to be because it uses default links to `Visual` for background and `NonText` for foreground. Although unfortunate, those are most likely have their own highlight groups that users can adjust.\r\n\r\nSo all in all, I think the choice for `NonText` is good enough here: it has to be one of the \"UI colors\" (shades of grey the same lightness as background) and relatively readable (so the one that is the most different from the background, which is `Grey4`).",
            "created_at": "2026-09-30T18:22:37Z",
